Ignore buffer modifiers when picking a plane on drivers without them

On a driver that does not advertise DRM_CAP_ADDFB2_MODIFIERS (virtio-gpu,
so any QEMU guest) no plane advertises modifier support either, so plane
allocation fails for every frame with "Could not find a suitable unused
DRM plane".

The framebuffer is already added without modifiers there, so match the
layer on format alone.

Signed-off-by: Mira <noreply@anthropic.com>

--- a/src/modesetting.c
+++ b/src/modesetting.c
@@ -2435,6 +2435,25 @@
     ASSERT_NOT_NULL(release_callback);
     ASSERT_EQUALS_MSG(deferred_release_callback, NULL, "deferred release callbacks are not supported right now.");
 
+    /*
+     * A driver that cannot do DRM_MODE_FB_MODIFIERS also does not advertise
+     * per-plane modifier support, so insisting on a modifier match here finds
+     * no plane at all and every frame fails with "Could not find a suitable
+     * unused DRM plane". virtio-gpu - i.e. any QEMU guest - is exactly this
+     * case.
+     *
+     * The framebuffer is already created without modifiers on such a device
+     * (see drmdev_add_fb_multiplanar_locked), so drop the modifier here too and
+     * let the layer be matched on format alone.
+     */
+    struct kms_fb_layer layer_without_modifier;
+    if (layer->has_modifier && !drmdev_supports_fb_modifiers(builder->drmdev)) {
+        layer_without_modifier = *layer;
+        layer_without_modifier.has_modifier = false;
+        layer_without_modifier.modifier = 0;
+        layer = &layer_without_modifier;
+    }
+
     if (builder->use_legacy && builder->supports_atomic && builder->n_layers > 1) {
         // if we already have a first layer and we should use legacy modesetting even though the kernel driver
         // supports atomic modesetting, return EINVAL.
